# Routing & Authentication

## React Router Setup

The application uses `react-router-dom` for navigation.

### Route Organization (client/src/App.tsx)

```typescript
<BrowserRouter>
  <AuthProvider>
    <Routes>
      {/* Public routes */}
      <Route path="/" element={<Index />} />
      <Route path="/signin" element={<SignIn />} />
      
      {/* Dashboard - Protected routes */}
      <Route
        path="/dashboard"
        element={
          <ProtectedRoute>
            <DashboardLayout />
          </ProtectedRoute>
        }
      >
        <Route index element={<Dashboard />} />
        <Route path="contacts" element={<Contacts />} />
        <Route path="prospect-hub" element={<ProspectHub />} />
        {/* ... other child routes */}
      </Route>
      
      <Route path="*" element={<NotFound />} />
    </Routes>
  </AuthProvider>
</BrowserRouter>
```

## Authentication (AuthContext)

Location: `client/src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx`

The application uses JWT-based authentication. The `AuthProvider` manages:
- Current user state (`user`).
- Authentication status (`isAuthenticated`).
- Initial session validation.
- Login and logout methods.

### Accessing Auth State

```typescript
import { useAuth } from "@/contexts/AuthContext";

const { user, isAuthenticated, isLoading, login, logout } = useAuth();
```

## ProtectedRoute

Location: `client/src/components/ProtectedRoute.tsx`

Guards routes that require the user to be logged in.

```typescript
import { ProtectedRoute } from "./components/ProtectedRoute";

// Usage in App.tsx
<Route
  path="/protected-path"
  element={
    <ProtectedRoute>
      <MyProtectedComponent />
    </ProtectedRoute>
  }
/>
```

### Behavior
- If `isLoading` is true, it usually shows a loading state.
- If `isAuthenticated` is false, it redirects to the sign-in page.
- If authenticated, it renders the children.

## OAuth Callbacks

The project includes several callback routes for third-party integrations:
- `/auth/callback`: General auth callback.
- `/calendar/callback/google`: Google Calendar integration.
- `/auth/google-contacts/callback`: Google Contacts import.
- `/auth/microsoft/callback`: Microsoft Contacts import.

## Navigation Patterns

Use `useNavigate` for programmatic navigation:

```typescript
import { useNavigate } from "react-router-dom";

const navigate = useNavigate();
navigate("/dashboard/contacts");
```

Use `Link` for declarative navigation:

```typescript
import { Link } from "react-router-dom";

<Link to="/dashboard">Go to Dashboard</Link>
```

